"P193089852" "From what I've heard, Marauder is the most dedicated of Emperor Cole's lackeys. I'm happy he's back behind bars for now. Having a cell of Praetorians right here in Paragon City is extremely dangerous."
// RandomFameString :
"P1764315414" "{HeroName} dispersed a Praetorian base on Peregrine Island!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Compound5.1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Fixadine 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1931372829" "Fixadine"
// DetailString :
"P932163700" "This Praetorian drug is quite similar to your world's Superadine, but there are certain subtle molecular differences. These differences could help Dr. Steven Sheridan isolate the components of Superadine that turn its users into Trolls."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P522879234" "Today I've got a chance for you to not only strike the Praetorians, but also do some good for this world. I've received word that the villain Dominatrix is having a rave in a warehouse on Praetorian Earth. Her guests will be enjoying all the most extravagant debauchments Praetorian Earth has to offer, including a drug called Fixadine. Sound familiar? That's because it's the Praetorian version of Superadine. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>I need you to defeat Dominatrix and confiscate the Fixadine.</A> Can you do it?"
// AcceptString :
"P3986349454" "Defeat Dominatrix and confiscate the Fixadine"
// SendOffString :
"P3806781044" "Fixadine and Superadine have some subtle molecular differences. Dr. Steve Sheridan believes he can use the Fixadine in his ongoing efforts to cure the Trolls of their Superadine-induced mutations. Once you've got the drug, get it over to him."

