"P4047289342" "Take Fixadine to Dr. Sheridan"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3662354241" "Dr. Sheridan is waiting on that Fixadine."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4015940964" "Ah, the Fixadine. Good. This should help my Superadine studies tremendously. Thank you, {HeroName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P409811342" "Great job, {HeroName}. Just terrific. Not only did you do something good for science, you also weakened Dominatrix's hold over her minions. Dominatrix leads through the strength of her personality and her followers' blind faith. Now that you've made her look weak before them, I doubt it'll be easy for her to maintain her position."
// RandomFameString :
"P1637507016" "I hear {HeroName} slugged it out with that Praetorian, Dominatrix!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission6.1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2047911462" "Chimera. Manticore's evil twin as it were. He's just as big a mystery in Praetoria as he is on this world, but a woman named Belladonna knows exactly where to find him. Turns out she used to be one of his assassins, but now she's part of the Resistance. We can portal you in directly into the training facility and you can <A HREF={ACCEPT}>take down Chimera and drag him back here for incarceration.</A> Simple job, but he is extremely deadly, so bring some help."
// AcceptString :
"P2720683942" "Take down Chimera at his training facility"
// SendOffString :
"P861494761" "Chimera's ninjas are stealthy and smart. You'll have to be the same if you want to succeed."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P4030982470" "Defeat Chimera & his guards"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P820089563" "That training facility was still in operation last time I checked."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2785993282" "Chimera's training facility is hidden away in this forgotten graveyard."
// Script Variable MISSION_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P68809674" "You shall not touch Chimera!"
// Script Variable MISSION_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P1824126240" "Taste swift death!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P353649114" "<shout>Chimera has been felled!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P60698443" "<shout>We will avenge Chimera!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3402193666" "<shout>Chimera's defeat will never be known!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2504386392" "You will pay for your insolence!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1146627913" "No one defeats Chimera and lives!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1953582092" "You will never speak of your success today!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2472695946" "You must be silenced!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3910612068" "Chimera"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2471163246" "Always remember, it is not just skill I teach you. It is a way of life."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1587214202" "Your strength cannot compete with my skill!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Chimera 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4031585324" "You defeated Chimera."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1563161096" "That ninja camp you shut down was one of Praetorian Earth's best facilities for churning out smart, well-trained troops. With it gone, we can all breathe a little easier. We've got Chimera contained as best we can in the Zig. Some days I wish we could go back to the Cold Storage method of containing the really awful villains. It kept Reichsman off the street for the longest time."
// RandomFameString :
"P3194270206" "I heard {HeroName} took on a whole camp of ninjas!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission7.1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P136634329" "Intel keeps rolling in on the Praetorians. They have an analogue of Citadel named Siege who oversees their Imperial Clockwork maintenance. We've got word that he's currently outside the City Maintenance Facility and overseeing some final prep on what they are calling 'WarWorks'. It could be a trap to draw out the Resistance and powerful heroes like yourself, but I think you can handle whatever they are throwing your way. Siege used to have a body that was similar to Citadel's, but he long since abandonded it once the new model Clockwork bodies came online. Now he hops from shell to shell for whatever he feels is appropriate for the job at hand. I need you to <A HREF={ACCEPT}>go in and destroy any and all WarWorks you find, including Siege if possible, and disable any power generators they have in the area.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P3324720249" "Take down the WarWorks"
// SendOffString :
"P3172166551" "My sources have informed me that the facility has several power generators you'll need to disable. <br><br>And if those WarWorks really are as powerful as intel suggest, I'd bring along some friends as well."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P642104358" "Defeat Siege and all Warworks"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2162324667" "If Siege isn't destroyed we've got a real problem on our hands."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3539812326" "Taking dimensional portals sometimes leaves a bad taste in your mouth."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P1476172860" "Siege"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYINFO :
"P1675154571" "Siege, the Praetorian version of Citadel, has long since abandoned his old body and now uses whatever shell is appropriate for the job at hand."
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3387703676" "Warworks coming on-line."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3883230806" "Primal incursion detected."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Generators 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P2334909622" "Power generator"
// Description :
"P1329004192" "generators to destroy"
// SingularDescription :
"P3397229729" "Destroy last generator!"
// InteractBeginString :
"P919493879" "You begin to destroy the generator."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P3976850122" "You have destroyed the generator."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2343706832" "You disabled Siege and his Warworks."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P343274135" "You've put a serious crimp in Siege's production. These Warworks seem very powerful, I shudder to think what they will ultimately be used for."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission8.1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P711857915" "Are you familiar wiht the Praetorian version of Luminary? She calls herself Nightstar, and she's a self-aware robot like Siege, only she seems a little bit crazy. She believes her power comes from a place called 'the Black Shroud', another dimension that she recently gained access to.<br><br>We have gotten word from the resistance that she is making her monthly pilgramage to the Black Shroud dimension, and this would be a perfect time to strike, taking her down without fear of Praetorian reprisal. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>We need you to go to the Black Shroud dimension and take down Nightstar,</A> can you pull this off for us, {HeroName}?"
// AcceptString :
"P1915502073" "Go to the Black Shroud dimension and take down Nightstar"
// SendOffString :
"P246727370" "You'll want to check the rooftops for Nightstar and her minions. That's where they can usually be found."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1418363883" "Take down Nightstar"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4234005495" "This is our best time to strike!"
// TaskTitle :
"P1421454009" "Black Shroud Dimension"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P761155658" "The Black Shroud dimension is cloaked in eternal night. Strange forces are at play here."
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2809604588" "You will find glory in Nightstar!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1868936624" "Nightstar will bring you happiness"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P120420005" "There is joy in following Nightstar"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3641477774" "Nightstar's power is boundless!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P544188665" "Bring on the Night(star)!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3964876210" "Nightstar"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1884960167" "These nights keep me sane. They keep me in touch with my power."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P416703047" "I have the power of the Black Shroud! It will be more than enough to finish you!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Nightstar 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P1236364332" "Defeat Nightstar & her guards"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P465851554" "You defeated Nightstar."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2989806117" "So, Nightstar really believes that she possesses the power of an entire dimension? Well, I guess for all I know, it could be true. After all, there are more things in Paragon City than are dreamt of in your philosophy, {HeroName}. True or not, Nightstar will be licking her wounds for a time. You've weakened a big threat, my friend; you should be proud."
// RandomFameString :
"P3038584454" "{HeroName} took on Nightstar, that Praetorian android!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Compound9.1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Inscription 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2950698212" "Stone"
// DetailString :
"P317003013" "The inscribed obelisk read: <br><br>'A gift, to our daughter Battle Maiden, from your loyal subjects on Warrior Earth. You are truly the greatest of us, and we will serve you faithfully unto death."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P641781505" "The Praetorian known as Battle Maiden is the counterpart to our very own Valkyrie. They both derive their power from the weapons strapped to their backs, weapons which came from an alternate dimension known as 'Warrior Earth'. We know that Battle Maiden is currently on Warrior Earth, but getting to that dimension is a bit tricky. She has in her lair an obelisk that when activated will give us the window we need to open a Portal to Warrior Earth. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>I need you to get to that obelisk and activate it, then get back here and we can get you to Warrior Earth.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P2897800696" "Go activate Battle Maiden's obelisk"
// SendOffString :
"P2059840921" "Battle Maiden's guards all come from Warrior Earth, not Praeotria."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Compound9.1_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2181999901" "Find the obelisk"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4235419417" "We need to get to Warrior Earth."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3316390413" "The dampness of the cavern walls tells you you're deep within the Earth."
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3263747481" "Battle Maiden has made her departure."
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2059769031" "Excellent. We have need of new troops."
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3831055155" "You will not follow Battle Maiden!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Obelisk 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P3784420011" "Obelisk"
// InteractBeginString :
"P467184865" "You begin to activate the obelisk."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P2723809544" "The obelisk has been activated."
// InteractActionString :
"P2802120437" "Activating..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2340970234" "You feel the dimensional barrier to Warrior Earth fall temporarily."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3825430001" "The obelisk has been activated, report to Tina Macintyre."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Compound9.1_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2647153364" "Take stone to Tina Macintyre"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1252835126" "Tina Macintyre needs to be informed that a portal can now be opened."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1484542166" "Maria phoned me and told me you'd be here to have me open a portal to Warrior Earth. We've been trying to do so but some sort of barrier was preventing the portal from working. However, just mintues ago something changed that allowed the portal to open.<br><br>Your doing I suppose?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Compound9.1_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P156039958" "Defeat Battle Maiden & her guards"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P286154316" "Battle Maiden can't be allowed to swell her army! She's already dangerous enough as it is!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1916773503" "It looks like Warrior Earth has seen better days."
// Script Variable NEGOTIATOR_ONE_INACTIVE_TEXT :
"P2475129974" "I think you'll find Battle Maiden's offer quite reasonable."
// Script Variable NEGOTIATOR_ONE_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P281170208" "The weapons are nice, true. But who do we get to fight?"
// Script Variable NEGOTIATOR_TWO_INACTIVE_TEXT :
"P3635885069" "Ah! A excellent opportunity for you to prove your combat skills."
// Script Variable NEGOTIATOR_TWO_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P3766681173" "Very well. Attack!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2255141394" "Vanda"
// Script Variable BOSS_TWO_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2807008467" "Jumali"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P1876743934" "Battle Maiden"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1288761020" "Take these weapons and use them in my service."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2140400178" "Do not interfere!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - BattleMaiden 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Weapons 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P3679303079" "Weapons rack"
// Description :
"P3270633964" "weapons to destroy"
// SingularDescription :
"P2618345563" "Destroy the last weapons!"
// InteractBeginString :
"P3928138324" "You begin to destroy the weapons."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P1227243418" "You have destroyed the weapons."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1124042012" "You defeated Battle Maiden."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1537549912" "By destroying those weapons, you upset Battle Maiden's delicate negotiations. I think it's safe to say that Warrior Earth won't be sending any more troops her way, at least for a while. From what we can tell of that world's warriors, not one of them wants to join up with a losing team."
// RandomFameString :
"P3288973867" "The word around Portal is that {HeroName} defeated Battle Maiden!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission10.1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P855163049" "The late Sister Psyche's Praetorian counterpart is called Praetor Tilman by those who back Cole's regime, and Mother Mayhem by those who oppose it. The reason I'm telling you this is that SHE'S ATTACKING PARAGON CITY RIGHT NOW!<br><br>Sorry, I'm in sort of panic mode right this second. She's over in Waxahachie Business Park with a whole slew of those creepy Seers and IDF soldiers. I don't know what her ultimate plan is, but she's definitely up to something to come to our world.<A HREF={ACCEPT}> I need you to get to that business park and take her down.</A> You are our best hope in stopping whatever she has cooked up."
// AcceptString :
"P2810350916" "Stop Mother Mayhem"
// SendOffString :
"P3685707644" "You'll need to take the Monorail to get to Waxahachie Park. Remember, Mother Mayhem's Seers are brainwashed psychics from Praetoria. Most of them don't even know a life outside of being one of her psychic puppets."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3418172905" "Defeat Mother Mayhem"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4179389192" "Waxahachie Park is still in the grip of Mother Mayhem and her Seers!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// LocationName :
"P993677580" "Waxahachie Park"
// EntryString :
"P4173411663" "Upon exiting the monorail you have a splitting headache."
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - PlayTogetherMission 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable HOSTAGE_NAME :
"P2929828946" "Sgt. Marcian"
// Script Variable HOSTAGE_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3812123410" "Help me out here, {HeroName}!"
// Script Variable HOSTAGE_ACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1705291957" "Over here!"
// Script Variable CAPTOR_NAME :
"P215645740" "Augur"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P1391281983" "Mother Mayhem"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1454953412" "Such an untapped wellspring of psychic potential!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P408322489" "Your mind will be delicious, {HeroName}!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - MotherMayhemDefeated 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P445437437" "You've stopped Mother Mayhem and pieced together her plan"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2929804971" "You defeated Mother Mayhem."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4086747595" "Wow, Tilman must be desperate to come to Primal Earth looking for more psychics. I'll have to let the Resistance there know they are putting a dent in her armor. They need some good news right about now."
// RandomFameString :
"P1298703502" "Did you see those Seers in Waxahachie Park? Creepy!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission11.1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mutagen 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P37455549" "Mutagenic drugs"
// DetailString :
"P3236134241" "Malaise planned to use these drugs to reverse the mutations of the Lost who have become full-fledged Rikti. By converting these people back into the Lost, Malaise hoped to cause chaos within the Rikti ranks and perhaps create new soldiers to return to Praetoria with."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2079296432" "One thing that Praetoria has no counterpart to our world with is the Rikti. Since the Rikti are not from outer space but from another dimension, they could have just as easily invaded Praetoria as here, and the Rikti can only invade one dimension at any given time, get it?<br><br>Yeah it's kinda complicated I know, but eventually you wrap your head around this stuff.<br><br>The reason I bring this up is because Malaise, the Praetorian one- not our version, seems to be waging a war against the Rikti right in our sewer networks. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>I'd like you to go into the sewers, find Malaise and put a stop to whatever plan he's cooked up.</A> Whatever it is, it can't be good for Paragon City."
// AcceptString :
"P2791131457" "Stop the battle between Malaise and the Rikti"
// SendOffString :
"P3711393668" "Malaise is the thrall of Mother Mayhem, so expect a heavy Seer presence in the sewers."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1602071300" "Defeat Malaise"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3451112943" "With all the gas pipes running through that sewer annex, you're courting disaster by letting that battle continue."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2750825829" "The maddened screams of tortured Rikti echo off the stone walls."
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3738806578" "Seer 9110"
// Script Variable BOSS_TWO_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2160361253" "Plektar"
// Script Variable BOSS_TWO_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2799655880" "Mind: Pain"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3351418995" "Seer 9111"
// Script Variable BOSS_TWO_DISPLAYNAME :
"P1298583651" "Lutki"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3544190908" "Malaise"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2443713052" "All is as planned!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1958403891" "Don't toy with me, {HeroName}!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - DefeatMalaise 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Drug 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P1363806637" "drug stashes to confiscate"
// SingularDescription :
"P4049653839" "Confiscate the last drug stash!"
// InteractBeginString :
"P4143148641" "You begin to confiscate the drugs."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P1374966550" "You have confiscated the drugs."
// InteractActionString :
"P3948062759" "Confiscating..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2426538523" "You stopped the battle in the sewers."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P349578520" "The Praetorian version of Malaise is one twisted individual. I shudder to think if that could have been our Malaise if Sister Psyche hadn't gotten to him first."
// RandomFameString :
"P1284248783" "{HeroName} fought Malaise in the sewers!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission12.1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Quill 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3398534337" "Quill of Jocas"
// DetailString :
"P767230358" "The Praetorian version of the Dagger of Jocas, which was used by the Midnight Squad to imprison Rularuu by creating the Shadow Shard. Each quill is able to sever the shadow essence of a living being which can then be taken to Shadow Earth where Black Swan absorbs it, renewing her power."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3908458174" "Black Swan is somewhat of an enigma. A few years back she was a major player in Praetoria, but her power seems to have waned in the meantime. It is apparent that Emperor Cole has a stranglehold on the Magic of Praetoria, so Black Swan is taking whatever she can get. She seems to strengthen her power by visits to an alternate dimension known as the Shadow World. We need you to <A HREF={ACCEPT}>go to the Shadow World and find out what she is doing to keep her power, and take her down if possible.</A> Cutting off her power supply will deal a huge blow to the Praetorian power base."
// AcceptString :
"P558696706" "Cut off Black Swan's source of power"
// SendOffString :
"P3519325579" "She's doing something to gain more power, we just need to determine what."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P24088773" "Defeat Black Swan, find her power source"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3590445782" "I need you to stop whatever it is Black Swan is doing."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P30471918" "Shadow Earth eerily resembles the Shadow Shard."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3205587882" "Black Swan"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P4170697671" "Yes, give me more power!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1839784496" "You are too late, {HeroName}. Jocas has severed the shadows and I have basked in their essence. And now you die!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - BlackSwan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P3865049458" "Defeat Black Swan"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2549199767" "Black Swan is holding an odd looking quill in her hand. It feels VERY powerful."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2264150707" "You defeated Black Swan and recovered one of her powerful quills."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P505414486" "So it seems that the Dagger of Jocas is different in Praetoria and Black Swan got her hands on the Quills of Jocas? I assume that's how she made the Shadow World, which resembles the Shadow Shard that the Midnight Squad made with the Dagger. She must absorb the shadows of her victims to power herself and create her minions at the same time. Excellent work, {HeroName}!"
// RandomFameString :
"P3300098289" "Maria Jenkins said that {HeroName} defeated Black Swan!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Errand1.1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2709573013" "Tyra-, err 'Emperor Cole' has taken to sending scouts of his Warworks robots into Peregrine Island recently. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>I need you to run a patrol sweep, tagging the patrol boxes as you go, to check for any Warwork incursions.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P612683607" "Run a patrol for Warwork activity"
// SendOffString :
"P3335279897" "If you see anything, and I mean anything, we need to know about it."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P402341530" "Patrol, watch for Warworks"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1478693744" "You haven't completed that patrol yet."
// Script Variable LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P594745901" "His power, like his Empire, knows no bounds!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4240192878" "You have ensured Peregrine Island's safety."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4217256481" "Thanks for doing your part to keep Peregrine Island safe. Make no mistake about it, if the Praetorians ever manage to mount an invasion, Peregrine Island will be ground zero. It's up to heroes like you to make sure they can't get a foothold on the area."
// RandomFameString :
"P2739098921" "{HeroName} knows the importance of protecting Peregrine Island."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2215636495" "You may be aware, {HeroName}, that Portal Corporation has faced down some serious threats form the dimension they've designated Upsilon Beta 9-6. Otherwise known as Praetorian Earth. It's a dimension ruled by brutal supervillains who seem intent on claiming our world for their own. Portal scientists has done a lot of research into the Praetorian dimension, and they believe they've identified weaknesses for each of the Praetorian supervillains. I'm about to send you on some of the most critical missions you'll ever carry out. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>You've got to battle this new threat at its source: Praetorian Earth.</A><br><br>The dangers you face on that world will be monstrous. I'd recommend always bringing a few friends along for backup."
// SendOffString :
"P3328414343" "Your first task is to prevent the villain Infernal from summoning more demons to bind within his spectral armor. I need you to get to Infernal's lair and destroy his summoning altar."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Altar 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3087070787" "The Praetorian Diabolique gains her power by controlling the spirits of the dead. I've got it on good authority that she's performing such a summoning in a graveyard on Praetorian Earth within the next few hours. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>If you could stop her before she enslaves the spirits in that graveyard, you'll have struck a solid blow in the fight to keep Paragon City safe.</A> You only have 2 hours to stop the summoning."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2360899345" "Defeat Diabolique & her minions"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1702869259" "You feel for the people who live in these homes, under the iron rule of Tyrant's Praetorians."
// Script Variable CEREMONY_INCANTING_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3300602222" "Let the dead be bound!"
// Script Variable CEREMONY_INCANTING_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2740744690" "You will not disrupt our mistress' ritual!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Diabolique 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Ghostie1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P3583000025" "Ghost"
// Description :
"P2801634426" "spirits to rescue"
// InteractCompleteString :
"P3090458323" "Your world is lucky to have heroes such as you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Ghostie2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P2556167384" "Thank you, my dear. I didn't relish the thought of serving that cold-hearted villain."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Ghostie3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P2858710142" "If you hadn't come along, we would have been hers forever!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3742550212" "You defeated Diabolique and rescued the spirits she planned to enslave."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P941425232" "Diabolique has enslaved some spirits."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4212117320" "Diabolique's spectral forces remain a force to be reckoned with, but at least you kept her from swelling their ranks. And you helped some people, too. Or should I call them ghosts? Spirits? Whatever you call them, you kept them free from Diabolique's rule. I'd say that's what being {HeroAdjective} is all about."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4166058285" "I know you tried, {HeroName}, but Diabolique still managed to enslave some of those spirits. I guess there's only one way to free them from her tyranny now: defeat Diabolique, once and for all. Maybe someday you'll get your chance."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - HolyWater 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P656594192" "Portal Corporation has located the stronghold of the Praetorian villain called Shadowhunter. It's a wooded thicket, where the bones of Shadowhunter's victims are kept, unburied and unconsecrated. Shadowhunter and his wolves draw their power from those bones, and from the restless spirits tied to them. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>If you could go to Shadowhunter's lair and consecrate the bones, you'll free the spirits of his victims.</A> Each spirit you free will weaken Shadowhunter and his minions. <br><br>There's a catch, though. If you don't manage to complete your mission quickly, Shadowhunter's wolves may get a chance to hide them. Then we'll never break his power. You only have 1 hour."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P56405346" "Defeat Shadowhunter & his wolves"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2540267125" "You move toward Shadowhunter's lair, careful to remain downwind."
// Script Variable PATROLLER_ATTACK_DIALOG1 :
"P3511359874" "Ayoooah!"
// Script Variable PATROLLER_ATTACK_DIALOG2 :
"P2477542518" "Wooohhhaah!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2888469689" "Shadowhunter"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P214892298" "On whom shall we feast tonight, my brothers?"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P4025886115" "These woods, and everything in them, are mine!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Shadowhunter 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Bones 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3964098472" "You defeated Shadowhunter and consecrated the bones of his victims."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2490438953" "Shadowhunter's minions spirited away the rest of the bones."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3862123572" "Good work, {HeroName}. It'll take Shadowhunter a long time to recoup the power you took from him. I suspect we won't be hearing from him for a while!"
// RandomFameString :
"P2700722061" "I hear {HeroName} went up against the Praetorian villain, Shadowhunter!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P357156942" "Hmm. Shadowhunter and his minions seem to have hiden the remains of his victims. There's a chance we'll never get another chance to weaken him. But we'll keep looking, {HeroName}. I promise you that."
// RandomFameString :
"P1652035755" "I hear {HeroName} got tricked by Shadowhunter!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1387526514" "Hold onto your hat, {HeroName}. I've got a lead on a Praetorian incursion into Paragon City itself. It seems that Marauder has set up a military base over on Peregrine Island! I don't have to tell you that there are a lot of valuable military targets on that island. Nor do I have to tell you how quickly this situation could become deadly. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>You've got to get to Peregrine Island and wipe out Marauder's cell.</A>"
// SendOffString :
"P506419367" "It may be that Marauder has a stable portal back to his home world. If so, you'll need to destroy it."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3562925072" "Defeat all villains in base"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3633576078" "Marauder's infiltration cell is the single greatest threat to Paragon City's security."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2348033218" "Serve Tyrant or die!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P733188508" "For Tyrant!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Portal 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P913616454" "Portal"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2397781408" "From what I've heard, Marauder is the most dedicated of Tyrant's lackeys. It's disturbing that he found his way into Paragon City and went so far as to set up a base. I've asked Portal Corporation to keep a tighter lock on any unauthorized portal activity. In the meantime, I hope you'll be prepared to help me defend Paragon City from any future invasions."

