// Script Variable LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P2412343907" "Thanks for ruining a great party!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission6 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2902709145" "We've located the primary facility where Chimera trains his ninja assassins. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>I'd like you to get in there and take down that training facility.</A> You'd wipe out a good portion of Chimera's troops, while making it harder for him to train others. That's what I'd call a big coup."
// AcceptString :
"P2127915793" "Take down Chimera's training facility"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Chimera 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2358003564" "That ninja camp you shut down was one of Praetorian Earth's best facilities for churning out smart, well-trained troops. With it gone, we can all breathe a little easier. I imagine Chimera's catching the brunt of Tyrant's temper right now; I know I wouldn't want to be him tonight!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission7 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Parts 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4124417901" "Android parts"
// DetailString :
"P1736137587" "You recovered these android parts from Siege's production facility on Praetorian Earth. They should help the scientists of your world figure out how to best combat Siege's legions."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2845844559" "This is exciting, {HeroName}. We've got a lead on one of Siege's primary reproduction facilities, the factories where he produces all his android minions.<A HREF={ACCEPT}> If you could get to Praetorian Earth and shut down Siege's factory, you'll be taking a lot of the bite out of his army.</A> It won't be easy, {HeroName}. But I believe that if anyone can manage this, it's you."
// AcceptString :
"P1230932206" "Shut down Siege's factory"
// SendOffString :
"P3885315308" "My sources have informed me that the facility has several power generators you'll need to disable."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1311615246" "Defeat Siege & his guards"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3625600143" "If Siege is allowed to keep pumping out robots, Paragon City could have hard times ahead."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1397324901" "Siege's massive factory spouts great gouts of black smoke into the air."
// Script Variable PATROLLER1_SEARCHING_DIALOG :
"P2290916232" "Siege has ordered increased production."
// Script Variable PATROLLER2_SEARCHING_DIALOG :
"P1331376737" "Excellent! Our army will be rivaled by none!"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2639376760" "We must step up production to prepare for the invasion."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P673443454" "My robot warriors will tear you to shreds!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Siege 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Parts 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P480797583" "Seek clues"
// InteractBeginString :
"P907740812" "You begin to examine the parts."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P395867287" "You have examined the parts."
// InteractActionString :
"P1412195360" "Examining..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1598184313" "You have found some of the parts used to create Siege's minions!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Generators 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2537920029" "You disabled Siege's factory and found some android parts."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P38131815" "You've put a serious crimp in Siege's production. Even better, these android parts you found should give us a good idea of how to best battle Siege's android doppelgangers. Citadel's been cooperating with us in our analyses of the androids, but there are still a few enigmas we can't crack. Maybe now that'll change."
// RandomFameString :
"P1029135482" "{HeroName} brought some android parts from Praetorian Earth!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission8 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2426512775" "Are you familiar with the Praetorian villain who calls herself Nightstar? I've heard some strange things about her. She's an intelligent robot, like Siege, but the difference is that she seems to be a little bit crazy. She believes that her power comes from a galaxy contained within her robotic armor. Every month, she goes out under the night sky to commune with the stars. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>If you could disrupt her ritual, her minions might start to doubt her.</A> Even more importantly, she might start to doubt herself."
// AcceptString :
"P2807784434" "Disrupt Nightstar's ritual"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2225347417" "Disrupt the ritual"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P27997364" "I really need you to disrupt Nightstar's ritual."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P66335057" "The night sky lends a strange peacefulness to Praetorian Earth."
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3132085771" "The sky is beautiful tonight."
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P4157850235" "Ssh. Is someone here?"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1506412962" "You will not disrupt our communion with the night!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3024790287" "To think. All Nightstar's power comes from the sky."
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3446791254" "Yes. She is truly a goddess."
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P516617798" "You are not fit to set eyes on Nightstar!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P19945262" "Do you see the way the stars sparkle more brightly for our mistress?"
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P640310086" "Ssh. Just let me enjoy it."
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2053483884" "You will be sorry you came!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3752975509" "The glow of the moon is most lovely."
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3199603163" "Yes. Just like our mistress."
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1886241975" "You cannot touch Nightstar's power!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2819811479" "I have the power of the stars! It will be more than enough to finish you!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Nightstar 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3548408988" "So, Nightstar really believes that she possesses the power of a galaxy. Well, I guess for all I know, it could be true. After all, there are more things in Paragon City than are dreamt of in your philosophy, {HeroName}. True or not, Nightstar will be licking her wounds for a time. You've weakened a big threat, my friend; you should be proud."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Compound9 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Inscription 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P880617415" "You scraped these stone shavings from the surface of an obelisk in Battle Maiden's lair. The inscribed obelisk read: <br><br>'A gift, to our daughter Battle Maiden, from your loyal subjects on Warrior Earth. You are truly the greatest of us, and we will serve you faithfully unto death."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3269125013" "We've learned that the Praetorian Battle Maiden is recruiting her troops from some other dimension. The problem is, we don't know which one. I need you to get to Praetorian Earth and infiltrate Battle Maiden's headquarters. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>See if you can find anything to indicate which world her troops are coming from.</A> If we can cut off her supply, we may be able to keep her from posing a threat to Paragon City."
// AcceptString :
"P3023853602" "Find out where Battle Maiden's troops are coming from"
// SendOffString :
"P1560434863" "If you find anything that might come from the world of Battle Maiden's troops, take it to Tina Macintyre. She may be able to get a dimensional trace on it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Compound9_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P510878993" "Find clue to Battle Maiden's plans"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3392503858" "We need to know where Battle Maiden's troops are coming from."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Obelisk 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractBeginString :
"P1866579175" "You begin to scrape away some stone."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P3427939487" "You have taken some stone from the obelisk."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1674791408" "This obelisk came from Battle Maiden's home world."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4199577609" "You found a clue to the source of Battle maiden's troops."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Compound9_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1468167358" "Tina Macintyre needs to see those stone shavings. She may be able to figure out their dimension of origin."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2619092075" "It certainly does look as though Battle Maiden is originally from this Warrior Earth. I wonder how she won a spot for herself among the Praetorians? If I had to guess, I'd say it was for her viciousness in battle. That's a trait that certainly seems to be valued in Praetorian society. <br><br>Let me see those stone shavings. Well, it's weak, but I've got a dimensional trace. I'll tell the technicians to open up a portal to Warrior Earth for you. Once you're there, you'll need to stop Battle Maiden from recruiting more troops."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Compound9_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - BattleMaiden 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Weapons 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission10 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P4009334301" "On our world, Sister Psyche's one of the nicest women I know. But on Praetorian Earth, her alter-ego is known as Mother Mayhem. Rather than use her psychic powers for good, Mother Mayhem uses them to drive people insane! She triggers the rage center in their brains, turning them into deranged killing machines. I've got an urgent report from Portal Corporation; Mother Mayhem and a slew of her 'patients' have just beamed into a downtown area called Waxahachie Park. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>You've got to get over there and stop Mother Mayhem!</A> Otherwise, the Waxahachie occupants may wind up dead! <color orange>You only have 2 hours to deal with the situation.</color>"
// SendOffString :
"P2564168307" "You'll need to take the Light Rail to get to Waxahachie Park. Remember, Mother Mayhem's minions are really just victims of her evil mind-control. Stop them, but don't do them harm."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2912318583" "Defeat all villains in area"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P336341394" "Waxahachie Park is still in the grip of Mother Mayhem and her deranged killers!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P4010451061" "You're shocked to realize that the wild, animal howls you hear actually come from human throats."
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3949319532" "Smash! Kill! Smash!"
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1533599795" "I like the pain! I like to destroy!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1465162203" "Rip you to pieces!"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1104474012" "Just a little tweak. There! Now their minds will explode with hatred!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2643446478" "You cannot save anyone here, {HeroName}!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4011563992" "Permanent damage has been done to Waxahachie Park."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3581165792" "The police rounded up Mother Mayhem's minions and took them to the asylum. The doctors there hope that after a few weeks away from Mother Mayhem's influence, those poor people may start to regain their sanity. I'd say you did a good thing not just for Paragon City, but for the oppressed people of Praetorian Earth as well."
// RandomFameString :
"P3113817691" "I'm treating one of Mother Mayhem's former minions. He never would have had a chance without {HeroName}!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2226022678" "Most of the people in that office park were able to hide from Mother Mayhem's goons; the rest were evacuated when the mayor sent in a hero clean-up squad. It looks like no lives were lost, but the damage done to the area was enormous. I'm afraid some of those businesses may not recover."
// RandomFameString :
"P287153980" "My office was totally trashed by Mother Mayhem and her psychotic goon squad!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission11 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mutagen 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3479289260" "Malaise planned to use these drugs to reverse the mutations of the Lost who have become full-fledged Rikti. By converting these people back into the Lost, Malaise hoped to cause chaos within the Rikti ranks and perhaps create new soldiers to swell his army."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P517829369" "The Rikti and the Praetorians may have the same goals in mind, but that doesn't make them friends. On the contrary. The Praetorians want to conquer Earth for themselves, so they're as interested in beating back the Rikti as we are. One of the Praetorians has cooked up an ingenious scheme for weakening the Rikti; Malaise plans to use some sort of drug to revert the converted Lost back to a more human state. He hopes to pit them against their Rikti masters and create chaos in the Rikti ranks. <br><br>As we speak, Malaise's forces are moving in on a Rikti base in the sewers. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>I need you to get to the sewers and stop the battle.</A> Damage to the sewer system is a real health hazard, and there's also the risk that Malaise will reinforce his army with the converted Lost."
// SendOffString :
"P3542909104" "Malaise has the power to inflict his madness on others; most of his minions are deranged and unstable, just like the Lost themselves. In fact, if he manages to revert some of the Rikti converts to their Lost state, they should fit right into his army."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P315776540" "Defeat all villains in sewer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P231987455" "The gibbering voices of Malaise's crazed minions bounce eerily off the sewer walls."
// Script Variable FIGHTER_ONE_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2264209143" "You gonna be like us!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_ONE_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P660092283" "Get 'em get 'em get 'em!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_DISPLAYNAME :
"P581700475" "Crazy Jake"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3792139566" "We make you better!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3900613448" "We make you dead!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_DISPLAYNAME :
"P1492715037" "Deranged Pete"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P4168106429" "Malaise says you'll be like us soon!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1688569930" "Die! Die! Die now!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_ONE_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1146153673" "Sick freaks! Disgusting!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_ONE_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P167896971" "Grraaaahahhh!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Drug 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4116214856" "It's disturbing how twisted Malaise's minions really are. I can't help but feel sorry for them; after all, they were ordinary people until Malaise got his hooks into them. At least you prevented him from converting the Rikti into more followers for his cause."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Mission12 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P408348504" "The Praetorian Black Swan gains her powers from her dimension of origin, some sort of Shadow World. No one at Portal Corporation has yet been able to determine which dimension Black Swan comes from, but we know that that's where she finds her shadow soldiers. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>If you could shut down Black Swan's portal to Shadow World, you could prevent her army from growing any larger.</A> Maybe you could even cut off her own power supply!"
// AcceptString :
"P573735058" "Shut down Black Swan's portal to the Shadow World"
// SendOffString :
"P39347445" "The location of this Shadow World is a mystery Portal Corporation has been trying to plumb for some time."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P592078323" "Defeat Black Swan & her guards"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P139622746" "I need you to shut down the portal linking Praetorian Earth to the Shadow World."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2493266763" "It seems that Black Swan and her shadow soldiers like to hang out in this crumbling graveyard."
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2538348627" "Prepare the portal for my departure."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2282062992" "How dare you come to my domain?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - BlackSwan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Portal 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P1375571128" "Destroy the portal"
// InteractBeginString :
"P3271577933" "You begin to destroy the portal."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4181800289" "You defeated Black Swan and destroyed her portal to the Shadow World."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2996424184" "We still haven't located Black Swan's Shadow World, but at least we've cut off her access to it for the time being. Good work, {HeroName}. I'm glad 'I've got you with me in the fight against the Praetorians."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Praetorians_Errand1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P709347924" "Ever since the Praetorians first set eyes on our dimension, they've wanted it for their own. It's only through the constant vigilance of heroes like yourself that Peregrine Island, the heart of Portal Corporation, is kept safe. If the Praetorians manage to take over Portal, we'll have no defense against their dimensional incursions. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>I'd like you to run a sweep through Peregrine Island and make sure there's no Praetorian activity going on.</A> "
// AcceptString :
"P1811435351" "Run a patrol for Praetorian activity"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1518844344" "Patrol, watch for Praetorians"
// Script Variable LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P239658719" "We'll take this island by force!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
